pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:1: # LLM serving control: evidence-driven project summary
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:2: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:3: Status: **research prototype; not Resume Ready for a real closed-loop MPC claim**.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:4: Evidence cutoff: 2026-11-04. Negative results are acceptable; unsupported claims are not.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:5: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:6: ## Problem and contribution
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:7: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:8: Heterogeneous prompts and output caps make request-count limits an imperfect
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:9: proxy for serving load. This project investigates admission decisions in front
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:10: of vLLM, balancing completed-request SLO goodput, overload rejection and latency.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:11: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:12: The original work is the gateway admission/accounting layer, lifecycle and
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:13: control-timing instrumentation, reproducible workload/audit tooling, and
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:14: experimental prediction, planning and guarded-actuation components. It is
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:15: **not** an implementation of vLLM's continuous batching, PagedAttention, model
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:16: kernels or KV-cache manager.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:17: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:18: The proposed controller observes versioned state, predicts candidate budget
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:19: trajectories, optimizes over a finite horizon, executes the first action and
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:20: reobserves. The actuator changes gateway reservation budget, not the native
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:21: engine's token budget. [Architecture](architecture.md) distinguishes working
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:22: subsystems from the unqualified integrated loop.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:23: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:24: ## Immediate evidence report
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:25: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:26: | Defensible now | Evidence and boundary |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:27: |---|---|
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:28: | Instrumented, audited real-GPU serving captures | E1: archived request outcomes, state reconstruction and applied-control timing. These are scheduled identification runs, not MPC runs. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:29: | Implemented finite-horizon policy-planning components | E2: independently accepted CPU/shadow tests. No native performance claim follows. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:30: | Implemented and tested observation/consumer deployment components | E3: bounded CPU integration evidence; subsequent D2-F1 blocks live release of that composition. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:31: | Preserved negative results and release blockers | E4/E5: incomplete native observation coverage and cleanup failure path; neither is relabelled PASS. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:32: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:33: Full traces, commands, configurations and exact commits are indexed in
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:34: [benchmark results](benchmark_results.md). Historical audits are not represented
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:35: as new replications performed for this document.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:36: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:37: ## MVP completion gate
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:38: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:39: P0 is complete only when all rows below have reviewable evidence. Winning every
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:40: baseline, convergence of the Native14 posterior, and production deployment are
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:41: **not** requirements.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:42: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:43: | Priority | Deliverable / acceptance | Current status |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:44: |---|---|---|
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:45: | P0 | Explain original work, actuator, states, model limitations, objective and constraints without conflating gateway and engine state. | Documented; final independent claim audit pending. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:46: | P0 | One runnable, source-pinned path demonstrating repeated real observation, prediction, optimization, first-action application and reobservation. Retain refusals, timeouts and actual applied-state evidence. | **Missing native end-to-end evidence.** Shadow output and ACK-only evidence do not qualify. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:47: | P0 | Safe bounded operation: queue/admission limits, overload outcomes, stale-state refusal, unknown-command handling, timeout cleanup and private-config handling. | Components tested; **D2-F1 repair/acceptance remains required** for the affected launcher. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:48: | P0 | Comparable descriptive GPU results for MPC, strong development-selected Fixed, FIFO and strong OneMove; same workload, model, resource limits and scoring. | **Not collected.** FIFO identity and missing throughput/fairness reporting require explicit resolution. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:49: | P0 | Report TTFT p50/p95/p99, SLO goodput, throughput, rejection, fairness and full controller overhead, with sample counts and failures. | Historical measurements are partial; current MPC table is unfilled. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:50: | P0 | Portable commands/configurations, raw-to-table reconstruction and exact code/data commits; audit every quantitative resume claim. | Historical bundles exist; clean-checkout MVP reproduction remains unverified. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:51: | P1 | Better decision-relevant forecasts, overhead reduction, broader workload/load coverage and repeatability estimates. | Only if a P0 result justifies the change. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:52: | P2 | Native14 mixing research, full empirical-pool quantiles, new proposal geometry, extensive posterior qualification, large confirmatory campaigns and additional hardware. | Separate research backlog; must not delay P0 or applications. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:53: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:54: A replacement simple frozen predictor is permissible only under its own
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:55: explicit experimental scope, support and validation. It cannot inherit
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:56: Native14 qualification, waive safety checks, or be presented as a calibrated
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:57: posterior. Existing scientific gates remain unchanged.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:58: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:59: ## Smallest remaining execution path
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:60: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:61: 1. Reuse accepted planner/accounting components. Resolve the known cleanup and
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:62:    scorer blockers; finish one small integration path, not another model family.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:63: 2. Freeze one MVP protocol: exact commands, state/action interface, baseline
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:64:    selection, FIFO meaning, workload, resource bounds, metric definitions,
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:65:    failure handling and stopping budget. Resolve portability before GPU work.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:66: 3. Perform one bounded real-loop engineering smoke. Require actual application
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:67:    and reobservation, not a same-budget no-op or simulated action receipt.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:68: 4. If the smoke passes, run the predeclared sequential policy comparison on the
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:69:    authorized GPU. Publish descriptive results even if MPC loses.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:70: 5. Reconstruct the table, audit claims, commit the evidence and declare
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:71:    **Resume Ready** only after P0 closes. Move all optional research to P1/P2.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:72: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:73: No experiment is launched by this document. Before each proposed run, Mayor must
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:74: record: the specific P0 claim it establishes, why existing evidence is
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:75: insufficient, fixed scope/budget, outcomes that stop work, and resulting
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:76: trace/config/command/commit. A run with no new P0 answer is deferred.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:77: The former open-ended iteration objective is superseded by this gate.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:78: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:79: ## Safe resume wording today
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:80: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:81: - Built an instrumented vLLM serving gateway and reproducible trace-replay
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:82:   tooling for admission-control and overload analysis, preserving request
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:83:   outcomes and auditable control-timing evidence.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:84: - Implemented and CPU-validated finite-horizon MPC planning components with
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:85:   versioned-state, deadline and failure checks; documented the remaining native
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:86:   closed-loop and baseline-comparison gaps.
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:87: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:88: These are prototype claims, not production deployment, guaranteed latency, or
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:89: MPC superiority. Role-specific alternatives are in [resume bullets](resume_bullets.md).
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:90: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:91: ## Seven-agent ownership
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:92: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:93: | Role | Bounded resume-focused responsibility |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:94: |---|---|
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:95: | Model Identification | State/parameter/model/support table tied to accepted evidence. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:96: | Sampling & Mixing | Estimation reproducibility and numerical limitations; no convergence campaign for P0. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:97: | Model Improvement | Only validated improvements that change or explain controller decisions. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:98: | Independent Validation | Claim ledger, leakage audit, counterexamples and unsupported wording. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:99: | MPC Planner | Objective, horizon, constraints, actions and Fixed/OneMove distinction. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:100: | Closed-loop Runtime | Actual first-action loop and bounded failure/cleanup behavior. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:101: | Fair Comparison | Comparable baseline definitions, metrics, overhead and all failure cases. |
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:102: 
pinned-docs/resume_project_summary.md:103: Mayor owns integration, acceptance, GPU serialization and local commits.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:1: # Serving and control architecture
pinned-docs/architecture.md:2: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:3: Status: implemented serving/instrumentation and CPU research components;
pinned-docs/architecture.md:4: the complete native MPC loop is **not yet qualified**.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:5: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:6: ```mermaid
pinned-docs/architecture.md:7: flowchart LR
pinned-docs/architecture.md:8:     W[Fixed offered workload] --> G[Gateway admission and reservation ledger]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:9:     G -->|admitted request| V[vLLM inference engine]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:10:     G -->|overload rejection| O[All-offered outcome log]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:11:     V -->|stream and terminal outcome| G
pinned-docs/architecture.md:12:     G --> T[Versioned lifecycle and control telemetry]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:13:     V -. experimental native observations .-> T
pinned-docs/architecture.md:14:     T --> Q[Clock, identity, freshness and coherence checks]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:15:     Q --> M[Frozen prediction model and shared scenarios]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:16:     M --> P[Bounded finite-horizon planner]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:17:     P --> A[First-action actuator and application check]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:18:     A -. native MPC integration not qualified .-> G
pinned-docs/architecture.md:19:     T --> O
pinned-docs/architecture.md:20:     O --> B[Offline audits and benchmark table]
pinned-docs/architecture.md:21: ```
pinned-docs/architecture.md:22: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:23: Solid arrows describe serving flow or implemented component interfaces, not
pinned-docs/architecture.md:24: proof that the full diagram has run as an integrated controller. The dashed
pinned-docs/architecture.md:25: actuator edge is the principal missing native closed-loop evidence.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:26: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:27: ## Ownership and extension points
pinned-docs/architecture.md:28: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:29: | Layer | Responsibility | Repository evidence |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:30: |---|---|---|
pinned-docs/architecture.md:31: | vLLM | Model execution, native batching and cache management. | External backend; do not claim these algorithms as project contributions. |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:32: | Gateway | Reservation accounting, admission/rejection, streaming lifecycle and cleanup. | [`gateway.py`](../gateway.py) |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:33: | Measurement | Scheduled arrivals, actual applications, request/state/diagnostic records. | [`trace_control.py`](../trace_control.py), [`telemetry.py`](../telemetry.py), E1 in [results](benchmark_results.md) |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:34: | Prediction/planning | Coherent scenario rollouts and policy selection. | [`mpc_lab/model.py`](../mpc_lab/model.py), [`mpc_lab/controller.py`](../mpc_lab/controller.py), E2 frozen planner |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:35: | Runtime/actuation | Observation guards, pending-command handling and first-action coordination. | [`mpc_lab/runtime.py`](../mpc_lab/runtime.py), [`mpc_lab/actuator.py`](../mpc_lab/actuator.py); native qualification pending |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:36: | Evaluation | All-offered scoring, failure retention and baseline accounting. | [`mpc_lab/benchmark.py`](../mpc_lab/benchmark.py), accepted research evidence; no completed current native comparison |
pinned-docs/architecture.md:37: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:38: The public library and frozen team16 prototypes are separate versions. Do not
pinned-docs/architecture.md:39: combine their settings, interfaces or test totals into one allegedly deployed
pinned-docs/architecture.md:40: implementation.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:41: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:42: ## State and actuator semantics
pinned-docs/architecture.md:43: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:44: Gateway observations include immutable request reservation costs, reserved work
pinned-docs/architecture.md:45: R, awaiting-first-content Q, streaming D, ages and arrival/outcome history.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:46: These are gateway state/proxies, **not observed remaining GPU work**.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:47: Native scheduler/copy-ready information needs its own source-clock and
pinned-docs/architecture.md:48: availability qualification.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:49: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:50: The controlled value is a gateway weighted reservation budget u. Admission
pinned-docs/architecture.md:51: requires `R + request_cost <= u`; terminal cleanup releases that request's
pinned-docs/architecture.md:52: reservation. A lower budget does not evict already admitted work. An increase
pinned-docs/architecture.md:53: does not itself submit a request. Gateway release is not proof that cancelled
pinned-docs/architecture.md:54: backend computation stopped.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:55: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:56: ## Prediction and optimization
pinned-docs/architecture.md:57: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:58: The reference specification maximizes expected completed SLO-good request count
pinned-docs/architecture.md:59: over a fixed offered cohort using a common scenario panel. Rejected, failed or
pinned-docs/architecture.md:60: unresolved requests receive no positive success credit. Candidate plans use the
pinned-docs/architecture.md:61: same model, objective, resource constraints and scoring population.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:62: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:63: Fixed holds one budget. Strong OneMove can choose the best permitted single
pinned-docs/architecture.md:64: transition, including a delayed transition; it is not a deliberately weak
pinned-docs/architecture.md:65: one-step forecast. MPC can consider multiple future actions but executes only
pinned-docs/architecture.md:66: the first, then reobserves. The accepted frozen planner's exact limits belong to
pinned-docs/architecture.md:67: its own PLAN, not a universal horizon setting.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:68: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:69: See the [mathematical specification](../experiments/mpc-research/mpc-mathematical-specification.md)
pinned-docs/architecture.md:70: and E2 for configuration-specific details. Native14 is a separate failed-
pinned-docs/architecture.md:71: qualification model; a source-faithful formula is not evidence of predictive
pinned-docs/architecture.md:72: accuracy or calibrated uncertainty.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:73: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:74: ## Runtime contracts and unresolved failure paths
pinned-docs/architecture.md:75: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:76: Reject stale, incoherent, wrong-clock or wrong-version observations. Bound
pinned-docs/architecture.md:77: search and account for observation, serialization, IPC, solver, logging and
pinned-docs/architecture.md:78: application delay. An unresolved command timeout means unknown application,
pinned-docs/architecture.md:79: not cancellation; do not send speculative replacements.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:80: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:81: Process exit must include owned roots/leaves/readers/helpers and a truthful
pinned-docs/architecture.md:82: final receipt. Pre-return metadata is not proof of completed cleanup. D2-F1
pinned-docs/architecture.md:83: currently shows how a pending alarm or failed cleanup-anchor publication can
pinned-docs/architecture.md:84: skip cleanup in one deployment composition. That launcher is not live-eligible
pinned-docs/architecture.md:85: until its repair is accepted.
pinned-docs/architecture.md:86: 
pinned-docs/architecture.md:87: Admission/resource bounds are not end-to-end latency guarantees, universal
pinned-docs/architecture.md:88: queueing stability, physical KV safety or production reliability certification.
