pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:68: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:69: No row above establishes calibrated prediction, actual MPC benefit, production
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:70: deployment, deterministic SLO compliance or a general OS cleanup theorem.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:71: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:72: ## Required MVP comparison: currently unmeasured
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:73: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:74: | Policy | TTFT p50/p95/p99 | SLO goodput | Throughput | Rejection | Fairness | Controller overhead |
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:75: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:76: | Strong development-selected Fixed | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured |
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:77: | Explicit FIFO baseline | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured |
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:78: | Strong OneMove | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured |
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:79: | Receding-horizon MPC | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured | Not measured |
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:80: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:81: The historical accepted comparison harness has no separate FIFO arm, throughput
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:82: metric or fairness index. These are P0 implementation/specification gaps, not
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:83: zero-valued measured results. FIFO is a queue discipline, not automatically a
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:84: distinct admission controller: define its hard bounds and distinguish it from
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:85: Fixed, or explicitly disclose identical arms.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:86: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:87: Before collection, freeze the strongest Fixed selection on development data
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:88: only; use identical action/resource support, offered requests, prompt/output
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:89: rules, warmup/cache settings and failure accounting across policies. OneMove
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:90: must use the same model/scenario panel and a meaningful best single-transition
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:91: search. Charge controller delays without slowing the offered workload to hide
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:92: overhead. Serialize GPU arms; record ordering, resets and contamination checks.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:93: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:94: Required metric definitions:
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:95: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:96: - TTFT: report scheduled-arrival and client-send origins separately, estimator,
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:97:   completed-request sample counts and missing/censored outcomes.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:98: - SLO goodput: successful, SLO-meeting completions divided by the fixed offered
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:99:   interval; every rejected/failed/unknown offer remains in the outcome ledger.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:100: - Throughput: declare completed requests/s versus output tokens/s and whether
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:101:   warmup/drain are included. Never substitute HTTP-record count for generations.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:102: - Rejection/failure: report each outcome over all offered requests, retaining
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:103:   unknown application and incomplete cleanup.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:104: - Fairness: predefine workload groups and report per-group offered-normalized
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:105:   SLO attainment/rejection. Define any Jain index, zero-denominator convention
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:106:   and group sample counts prospectively; no starvation guarantee follows.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:107: - Overhead: include observation, model, IPC, optimization, logging, actuation,
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:108:   missed deadlines and end-to-end delay; isolated CPU solver time is insufficient.
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:109: 
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:110: A descriptive pilot may support a bounded engineering claim without statistical
pinned-docs/benchmark_results.md:111: superiority. Do not turn that scope into a PASS on an older confirmatory gate.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:1: # Interview defense
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:2: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:3: Use the [evidence ledger](benchmark_results.md) with each quantitative answer.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:4: Current title: **LLM serving admission-control and MPC research prototype**.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:5: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:6: ## What did you build beyond vLLM?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:7: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:8: An admission/accounting gateway, workload replay and lifecycle audits, control-
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:9: application timing instrumentation, and experimental model/planner/runtime
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:10: components. vLLM supplies native inference, batching and KV management; those
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:11: are not my claimed inventions.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:12: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:13: ## What does the controller actually control?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:14: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:15: A positive weighted reservation budget at the gateway. It decides which new
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:16: requests may be admitted. It does not directly set native batch tokens, evict
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:17: active requests or guarantee the backend has stopped cancelled computation.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:18: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:19: ## What makes the design MPC rather than a threshold rule?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:20: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:21: It evaluates future action sequences against a prediction model and constrained
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:22: objective, executes the first action and reobserves before replanning.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:23: CPU/shadow planning exists; current evidence does not establish an integrated
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:24: native MPC deployment. A future complete-loop claim needs real application and
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:25: reobservation receipts.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:26: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:27: ## What is the objective?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:28: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:29: The reference specification maximizes expected eventual successful requests
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:30: meeting the TTFT SLO over a fixed offered cohort. Rejected and failed requests
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:31: cannot improve the score by disappearing. Tail/unresolved credit and tie
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:32: breaking must be fixed across policies. Settings are version-specific.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:33: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:34: ## What are the state and prediction limitations?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:35: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:36: Gateway reserved work, lifecycle phases and ages are observable proxies.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:37: Remaining GPU work is partly latent. Source time differs from availability.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:38: Native14 did not meet its sampling qualification; its uncertainty is not
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:39: calibrated. A source-faithful model or retrospective replay is not a validated
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:40: forecast or counterfactual action-ranking model.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:41: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:42: ## Why not require an elaborate Bayesian model for the MVP?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:43: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:44: MPC needs an explicit predictive model, not necessarily that model family.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:45: A simpler frozen experimental predictor may demonstrate the engineering loop
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:46: if separately scoped, checked and labelled. It cannot inherit qualification or
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:47: justify accuracy guarantees. Advanced mixing/quantiles belong in P2 unless
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:48: they answer a concrete P0 question.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:49: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:50: ## What is the difference from Fixed, FIFO and OneMove?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:51: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:52: Fixed holds a development-selected budget. FIFO specifies service order and
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:53: needs an explicit admission/resource policy; otherwise it may duplicate Fixed.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:54: Strong OneMove searches a best allowed single transition with the same model
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:55: and evaluation horizon. MPC permits more action changes and replans. Do not
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:56: weaken the baselines or give MPC privileged future information.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:57: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:58: ## Why report rejection next to tail latency?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:59: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:60: Successful-request latency can improve simply by rejecting hard requests.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:61: All-offered SLO goodput, rejection, throughput and group outcomes expose that
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:62: trade-off. Conditional p99 is descriptive, not a service-level guarantee.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:63: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:64: ## Where can tail latency come from?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:65: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:66: Admission waiting, backend scheduling/prefill/decode interference, transport,
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:67: event-loop stalls, GC and measurement delay. An overlapping pause is not
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:68: exclusive causal attribution. Separate scheduled-arrival, send, first-content,
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:69: terminal and application clocks.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:70: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:71: ## What failure handling matters?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:72: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:73: Versioned state, expiry checks, bounded planning, unknown-command fencing,
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:74: exact reservation release and owned-process cleanup. D2-F1 shows why truthful
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:75: failure reporting alone is insufficient when cleanup can be skipped. The
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:76: affected composition remains blocked pending repair.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:77: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:78: ## What do the existing measurements establish?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:79: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:80: E1 provides audited historical native serving measurements under scheduled
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:81: budgets; E2/E3 provide bounded CPU component evidence. E4 is a partial native
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:82: observation diagnostic. None establishes a fair native MPC win. A/B were on
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:83: different hosts and are not a causal policy comparison.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:84: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:85: ## What if MPC loses?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:86: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:87: Publish the actual table and scope, then explain model error, overhead, control
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:88: authority or workload sensitivity only where evidence supports the explanation.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:89: The accounting, instrumentation, bounded runtime and reproducibility remain
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:90: engineering contributions. A negative result is better than an inflated claim.
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:91: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:92: ## What would make this Resume Ready?
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:93: 
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:94: The P0 gate in [the project summary](resume_project_summary.md): a reproducible
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:95: real loop, safe failure paths, comparable descriptive baseline results and an
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:96: audited claim-to-trace/command/config/commit ledger. Superiority, production
pinned-docs/interview_defense.md:97: deployment and a universal SLO theorem are not prerequisites.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:1: # Resume bullets: verified prototype wording
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:2: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:3: Use **one** pair, not all six bullets. Current scope is a research prototype,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:4: not a completed native closed-loop MPC deployment. Evidence IDs refer to
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:5: [benchmark results](benchmark_results.md).
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:6: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:7: ## AI Inference / Infrastructure
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:8: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:9: - Built an instrumented vLLM admission-control gateway and trace-replay
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:10:   pipeline; audited native serving captures replaying 7,643 offered requests
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:11:   over 300 seconds, retaining overload rejections and control-timing evidence.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:12: - Implemented CPU-validated MPC planning components with versioned-state,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:13:   deadline and failure checks, documenting the remaining native integration
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:14:   and strong-baseline comparison gaps.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:15: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:16: Evidence: first bullet E1, including raw trace, collection configuration,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:17: reproduction command and publication/runtime commits; second bullet E2/E3/E5.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:18: The request count describes each historical identification capture, not MPC
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:19: throughput or a production traffic claim.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:20: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:21: ## Autonomous Systems / Runtime
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:22: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:23: - Designed a finite-horizon admission-control prototype with coherent scenario
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:24:   evaluation, first-action replanning interfaces and guarded command-state
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:25:   handling; validated planning components on CPU.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:26: - Built auditable observation, lifecycle and failure evidence for native LLM
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:27:   serving, distinguishing stale state, unknown application and incomplete
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:28:   cleanup from successful control.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:29: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:30: Evidence: E2/E3/E4/E5 and the [architecture](architecture.md). First-action
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:31: interfaces are not a claim that the complete native loop has been demonstrated.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:32: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:33: ## General Software / Distributed Systems
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:34: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:35: - Implemented an asynchronous inference gateway with reservation accounting,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:36:   overload handling and lifecycle telemetry for reproducible serving studies.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:37: - Developed source-pinned replay and independent validation workflows linking
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:38:   request outcomes, configurations and commands to Git revisions, preserving
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:39:   negative results and actionable runtime failure cases.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:40: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:41: Evidence: E1/E3/E4/E5. Do not substitute "production deployed" for "implemented".
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:42: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:43: ## Claims explicitly excluded
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:44: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:45: Do not claim MPC speedup, superior goodput, production use, guaranteed p99,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:46: bounded end-to-end latency, starvation freedom, native sampler convergence or
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:47: fully validated GPU scheduling. Do not combine CPU test totals across versions.
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:48: 
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:49: Once P0 closes, replace a prototype clause with the actual comparable result
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:50: and its evidence ID, whether positive, neutral or negative. Do not insert a
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:51: percentage until its numerator, denominator, workload, configuration, command,
pinned-docs/resume_bullets.md:52: trace and exact commit are reviewable.
